  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "The records collectively make the later strategy plausibly reconstructible. Multiple refractory-HEA studies already use high-energy or mechanical ball milling of elemental powders under argon followed by vacuum SPS, and R9 closely matches the short milling and approximately 1000°C SPS schedule, albeit for a different alloy. R1 and R4 show that milling plus SPS can generate fine-grained solid solutions and mixed BCC/FCC structures, while R1, R5, and R7 directly associate fine grains and solid solutions with grain-boundary and solid-solution strengthening. Other records establish milling-induced crystallite refinement and phase evolution. An expert could therefore propose applying short HEBM plus SPS to an equimolar Co-Cr-Fe-Ni-Ti alloy and expect nanocrystalline strengthening. The exact 83% FCC/17% BCC balance, Ti-specific thermodynamic explanation, and quantitative hardness and strength would not be directly predictable from these records."
